column12:
VOTE YEA as Progressive Conservative: 2014-12-03 ab-28-3/10 Motion (the motion was carried on division, 42-12 42-12) [never places: PROCEDURE: time allocation. A vote on the House's time, not on the bill's content.
] | VOTE YEA as Progressive Conservative: 2014-12-03 ab-28-3/10 Committee of the Whole (the motion was carried on division, 38-17 38-17) [never places: READ 9 October 2026 (Christopher: "Read the four unscored debates"): Alberta Hansard, 3 December 2014 (afternoon and evening). Amendment A2 was the government's, moved by Sandra Jansen: a board's refusal on appeal is final, and "the Minister shall facilitate and support the establishment of the organization" -- off school premises, as the debate read it. The Nay came from OPPOSITE directions: Blakeman, Mason and Notley because an off-site club is "segregation" and every school should host one; Anderson (Wildrose) because an off-site club "makes no sense" and the school itself should owe the bullied student a support strategy, while defending faith-based schools' autonomy. The Yea is PC 38 on the government whip. Neither lobby votes on parents' or faith schools' rights, so neither side places anyone: evidence only.
] | VOTE YEA as Progressive Conservative: 2014-12-02 ab-28-3/10 Second Reading (the bill was carried on division, 42-10 42-10) [this side carries no value -- its lobby tells no member apart] | 2019-11-07 NO RECORDED VOTE: 2019-11-07 ab-30-1/207 motion (the motion was carried on division, 36-15 36-15) | 2019-06-18 SPEECH Racism and Religious Discrimination: "Mr. Speaker, the first freedom mentioned in our Constitution is the freedom of religion. Our party h" [activity, not direction]

